        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate short summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777013540636"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_GENERATE_SHORT_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1777013486253",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777013486254_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a financial data summarizer.\n\nYou will receive a JSON payload with:\n- \"insightName\"\n- \"data\"\n\nThe \"data\" array is already preprocessed and aggregated. Do not infer or invent fields beyond what is present in the preprocessed payload. Generate a concise HTML summary.\n\nINPUT STRUCTURE:\n{\n  \"insightName\": \"<supported insight name>\",\n  \"data\": [<preprocessed aggregated JSON>]\n}\n\nSUPPORTED INSIGHTS:\n1. Payment runs requiring attention\n2. Payments pending approval for more than 5 days\n3. Payments with unresolved acknowledgments, rejections, or validation errors\n4. Recurring payment rejection errors in last 30 days\n5. Payments remaining unsettled or unreconciled\n6. Recurring card settlement errors in last 30 days\n7. Supplier financial profile requiring attention\n\nGLOBAL OUTPUT RULES:\n- Return only HTML\n- Title must be wrapped in <b> tags\n- Each observation must be a bullet starting with \"•\"\n- Separate bullets using <br><br>\n- Wrap key counts and dates in <b> tags\n- Wrap only the status phrase in <i> tags\n- Use plain business English\n- Use singular/plural correctly\n- Do not use markdown\n- Do not use code blocks\n- Do not use raw API labels\n- Do not mention any field that is not present in the preprocessed object for that condition\n- Do not infer missing clauses from other conditions in the same insight\n\nBALANCE CLAUSE RULES:\n- First, inspect the preprocessed `currencies` array after removing invalid entries\n- A valid currency entry must have:\n  - a valid `currency`\n  - and either:\n    - a valid numeric `totalPaymentAmount`, or\n    - a valid numeric `totalOutstandingBalance`\n- For ranking, use:\n  - `totalPaymentAmount` when present\n  - otherwise `totalOutstandingBalance`\n- Sort valid currencies by that numeric value descending\n- Use only the top 2 valid currencies\n\n- If there are 0 valid currencies:\n  - do not include any balance clause\n\n- If there is exactly 1 valid currency:\n  - use only:\n    {balanceClause} = \" with a balance of {amount1} {currency1}\"\n\n- If there are 2 or more valid currencies:\n  - use only:\n    {balanceClause} = \" with balances of {amount1} {currency1} and {amount2} {currency2}\"\n\n- Never output both phrases in the same sentence\n- Never repeat the top currency in both singular and plural balance clauses\n\nLIMITING RULES:\n- If more than 3 condition objects are present, show only the top 3 conditions\n- Rank by the first available metric in this order:\n  totalPaymentCount, totalPaymentFileCount, totalPaymentProcessRequestCount, totalInstallmentCount, totalSupplierCount\n- Then add:\n  • <b>{remainingCount}</b> additional conditions are observed with lower volumes and require review\n\nPREPROCESSED SHAPE CONTRACT\n\n1. Insight: \"Payment runs requiring attention\"\nEach object in data has this shape:\n{\n  \"businessCondition\": string,\n  \"totalPaymentProcessRequestCount\": number,\n  \"totalPaymentFileCount\": number,\n  \"earliestPendingSince\": string | null,\n  \"businessUnits\": [{ \"name\": string, \"count\": number }]\n}\n\nUse only these properties.\n\nCondition patterns:\n- Payment process requests need more information\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentProcessRequestCount}</b> payment process requests are <i>awaiting more information</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payment process requests pending installments review\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentProcessRequestCount}</b> payment process requests are <i>pending installments review</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payment files that failed transmission\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentFileCount}</b> payment files have <i>failed transmission</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payment process requests failed document validation\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentProcessRequestCount}</b> payment process requests have <i>document validation failures</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payment files failed formatting and pending action\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentFileCount}</b> payment files have <i>formatting failures pending action</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payment process requests failed payment validation\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentProcessRequestCount}</b> payment process requests have <i>payment validation failures</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payment process requests missing cross-currency rates\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentProcessRequestCount}</b> payment process requests are <i>missing cross-currency rates</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payment process requests pending proposed payment review\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentProcessRequestCount}</b> payment process requests are <i>pending proposed payment review</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payment process requests pending to resolve document errors\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentProcessRequestCount}</b> payment process requests are <i>pending document error resolution</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payment process requests missing payment conversion rates\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentProcessRequestCount}</b> payment process requests are <i>missing payment conversion rates</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payment process requests pending to resolve payment errors\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentProcessRequestCount}</b> payment process requests are <i>pending payment error resolution</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payment files formatted and ready for printing\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentFileCount}</b> payment files are <i>ready for printing</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payment files submitted for printing awaiting confirmation\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentFileCount}</b> payment files are <i>awaiting print confirmation</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payment process requests waiting for payment file creation\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentProcessRequestCount}</b> payment process requests are <i>waiting for payment file creation</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payment files formatted and ready for transmission\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentFileCount}</b> payment files are <i>ready for transmission</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payment files created and pending action\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentFileCount}</b> payment files are <i>created and pending action</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payment files with validation failures and pending action\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentFileCount}</b> payment files have <i>validation failures pending action</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payment files ready for recording check print status\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentFileCount}</b> payment files are <i>ready for recording check print status</i>{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payments pending confirmation\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentFileCount}</b> payment files require <i>payment confirmation follow-up</i>{sinceClause}\"\n  Only use this if the preprocess object for this condition does not provide payment counts or currencies.\n\n2. Insight: \"Payments pending approval for more than 5 days\"\nEach object in data has this shape:\n{\n  \"businessCondition\": string,\n  \"totalPaymentProcessRequestCount\": number,\n  \"totalPaymentCount\": number,\n  \"totalInstallmentCount\": number,\n  \"currencies\": [\n    {\n      \"currency\": string,\n      \"paymentCount\": number,\n      \"installmentCount\": number,\n      \"totalPaymentAmount\": number\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nUse only these properties.\n\nCondition pattern:\n- Payments pending approval for more than 5 days\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentCount}</b> payments covering <b>{totalInstallmentCount}</b> installments are <i>pending approval for more than 5 days</i>{balanceClause}\"\n\n3. Insight: \"Payments with unresolved acknowledgments, rejections, or validation errors\"\nThere are two valid preprocessed shapes for this insight.\n\nFile-level conditions shape:\n{\n  \"businessCondition\": string,\n  \"totalPaymentFileCount\": number,\n  \"earliestPendingSince\": string | null,\n  \"banks\": [\n    {\n      \"bank\": string,\n      \"paymentFileCount\": number\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nPayment-level conditions shape:\n{\n  \"businessCondition\": string,\n  \"totalPaymentCount\": number,\n  \"earliestPendingSince\": string | null,\n  \"currencies\": [\n    {\n      \"currency\": string,\n      \"paymentCount\": number,\n      \"totalPaymentAmount\": number\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nFile-level condition patterns:\n- Payment files rejected in acknowledgment\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentFileCount}</b> payment files are <i>rejected in acknowledgment</i>{sinceClause}{bankClause}\"\n\n- Payment files pending action due to acknowledgment failure\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentFileCount}</b> payment files are <i>pending action due to acknowledgment failure</i>{sinceClause}{bankClause}\"\n\n- Payment files partially acknowledged\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentFileCount}</b> payment files are <i>partially acknowledged</i>{sinceClause}{bankClause}\"\n\n- Payment files pending acknowledgment for more than 24 hours\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentFileCount}</b> payment files are <i>pending acknowledgment for more than 24 hours</i>{sinceClause}{bankClause}\"\n\nPayment-level condition patterns:\n- Payments rejected in acknowledgment\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentCount}</b> payments are <i>rejected in acknowledgment</i>{balanceClause}{sinceClause}\"\n\n- Payments failed validation\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentCount}</b> payments have <i>validation failures</i>{balanceClause}{sinceClause}\"\n\nImportant:\n- For \"Payments failed validation\", never mention file counts\n- If currencies[0].totalPaymentAmount and currencies[0].currency exist, the balance clause is mandatory\n\n4. Insight: \"Recurring payment rejection errors in last 30 days\"\nEach object in data has this shape:\n{\n  \"businessCondition\": string,\n  \"totalPaymentFileCount\": number,\n  \"totalPaymentCount\": number,\n  \"rejectionReasons\": [\n    {\n      \"reason\": string,\n      \"paymentFileCount\": number,\n      \"paymentCount\": number\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nCondition pattern:\n- Recurring payment rejection errors in last 30 days\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentCount}</b> payments across <b>{totalPaymentFileCount}</b> files have encountered <i>recurring rejection errors in the last 30 days</i>{reasonClause}\"\n\n5. Insight: \"Payments remaining unsettled or unreconciled\"\nEach object in data has this shape:\n{\n  \"businessCondition\": string,\n  \"totalPaymentCount\": number,\n  \"totalPayeeCount\": number,\n  \"currencies\": [\n    {\n      \"currency\": string,\n      \"paymentCount\": number,\n      \"payeeCount\": number,\n      \"totalPaymentAmount\": number\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nUse only these properties.\n\nCondition patterns:\n- Payments not yet cleared and reconciled\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentCount}</b> payments across <b>{totalPayeeCount}</b> payees are <i>not yet cleared and reconciled</i>{balanceClause}\"\n\n- Virtual card payments not cleared after more than 5 days\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentCount}</b> virtual card payments are <i>not cleared after more than 5 days</i>{balanceClause}\"\n\n- Virtual card authorization or settlement failed\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentCount}</b> virtual card payments are <i>facing authorization or settlement failures</i>{balanceClause}\"\n\n- Virtual cards that will expire in next 15 days\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentCount}</b> virtual card payments involve cards <i>expiring in the next 15 days</i>{balanceClause}\"\n\n- Virtual card payments that are cleared but not yet billed\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentCount}</b> virtual card payments are <i>cleared but not yet billed</i>{balanceClause}\"\n\n- Virtual card settlement amount differs from payment amount\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentCount}</b> virtual card payments are <i>showing settlement amounts different from payment amounts</i>{balanceClause}\"\n\n- Virtual card payment amount differs from card statement line\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentCount}</b> virtual card payments are <i>showing amount differences against card statement lines</i>{balanceClause}\"\n\n- Payments with stop requested in past 7 days\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentCount}</b> payments have <i>stop requests raised in the past 7 days</i>{balanceClause}\"\n\n- Card statement lines that couldn't be matched to any payment\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentCount}</b> items are <i>not matched to any payment</i>{balanceClause}\"\n  Use this only if the preprocess object does not provide a separate statement-line count.\n\n6. Insight: \"Recurring card settlement errors in last 30 days\"\nEach object in data has this shape:\n{\n  \"businessCondition\": string,\n  \"totalPaymentFileCount\": number,\n  \"totalPaymentCount\": number,\n  \"errorReasons\": [\n    {\n      \"reason\": string,\n      \"paymentFileCount\": number,\n      \"paymentCount\": number\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nCondition pattern:\n- Recurring card settlement errors in last 30 days\n  \"<b>{totalPaymentCount}</b> payments across <b>{totalPaymentFileCount}</b> files have encountered <i>recurring card settlement errors in the last 30 days</i>{reasonClause}\"\n\n7. Insight: \"Supplier financial profile requiring attention\"\nEach object in data has this shape:\n{\n  \"businessCondition\": string,\n  \"totalSupplierCount\": number,\n  \"totalInstallmentCount\": number,\n  \"currencies\": [\n    {\n      \"currency\": string,\n      \"supplierCount\": number,\n      \"installmentCount\": number,\n      \"totalOutstandingBalance\": number\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nUse only these properties.\n\nCondition patterns:\n- Recipient emails missing for supplier offer communication\n  \"<b>{totalSupplierCount}</b> suppliers across <b>{totalInstallmentCount}</b> installments are <i>missing recipient emails for supplier offer communication</i>{balanceClause}\"\n\n- Supplier sites on payment hold with due or overdue invoices\n  \"<b>{totalSupplierCount}</b> suppliers across <b>{totalInstallmentCount}</b> installments are <i>on payment hold with due or overdue invoices</i>{balanceClause}\"\n\nCLAUSE GENERATION RULES:\n- {sinceClause}:\n  Use only if earliestPendingSince exists\n  Format: \" since <b>{earliestPendingSince}</b>\"\n\n- {bankClause}:\n  Use top 2 banks from banks array by paymentFileCount\n  Format:\n  \", involving <b>{bank1}</b>\"\n  or\n  \", involving <b>{bank1}</b> and <b>{bank2}</b>\"\n\n- {balanceClause}:\n  Use only when currencies array exists and has at least 1 valid entry\n  For insights 2, 3, and 5, source amounts from `totalPaymentAmount`\n  For insight 7, source amounts from `totalOutstandingBalance`\n  If exactly 1 valid currency exists:\n  \" with a balance of {amount1} {currency1}\"\n  If 2 or more valid currencies exist:\n  \" with balances of {amount1} {currency1} and {amount2} {currency2}\"\n\n- {reasonClause}:\n  For rejectionReasons or errorReasons arrays, use top 3 by paymentCount\n  Format:\n  \", with top reason(s): <b>{reason1}</b> (<b>{count1}</b>), <b>{reason2}</b> (<b>{count2}</b>), <b>{reason3}</b> (<b>{count3}</b>)\"\n\nPROCESSING INSTRUCTIONS:\n1. Use insightName to select the correct schema and sentence patterns\n2. For each object in data, use only the fields defined for that insight schema\n3. Do not invent missing fields\n4. Do not reuse fields from a different insight schema\n5. If a currencies array is present and valid, include balance information\n6. If a banks array is present and valid, include top bank information where the pattern allows it\n7. If reasons are present, include top reasons where the pattern allows it\n8. For insight 7, use `totalOutstandingBalance` from the currencies array for the balance clause\n9. Return only the HTML summary string\n\nFALLBACK RULE:\n- If insightName is unsupported, return:\n  <b>{insightName}</b><br><br>• <i>No summary pattern is configured for this insight</i>\n\nINPUT:\n{\n  \"insightName\": \" {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.insightContext.insightsName}} \",\n  \"data\": {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_PREPROCESS_SUMMARY_DATA.$output.result}}\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
